 "The same idea — rules applied over time — runs a robot arm, a hurricane and an entire universe.": "94b13240a1e7.mp3",
 "What changes is the scale, and the physics engine underneath.": "320367eaabcb.mp3",
 "Robotics, measured in millimetres and milliseconds.": "afeb5fff99b0.mp3",
 "Robots are trained and tested in simulation long before they touch the real world.": "874c9d986944.mp3",
 "A virtual robot can fall a million times overnight without breaking a single motor — and learn to walk, grasp, or fly from those failures.": "650d94451051.mp3",
 "Environment, measured in kilometres and decades.": "2968c7bfb804.mp3",
 "Climate and weather models split the planet into a 3D grid of cells and solve the equations of fluid flow, heat and moisture in each one.": "bb40a1a9350a.mp3",
 "Ecosystem models add living things — forests, fish, fires — that react to that changing world.": "572042cf8907.mp3",
 "Universe, measured in megaparsecs and billions of years.": "138779f936de.mp3",
 "Cosmological simulations start with a nearly smooth early universe and let gravity do the rest.": "add369ab28ee.mp3",
 "Billions of particles of dark matter and gas clump into a cosmic web, then into galaxies, stars and black holes.": "2bea8a8c386b.mp3",
 "A physics engine is the heart of a simulation: the code that decides how things move, collide and push on each other.": "a24a498f8a77.mp3",
 "Strip away the details and nearly every engine runs the same loop, many times per simulated second.": "61b1d57fd3d3.mp3",
 "Step 1: Apply forces.": "5605c4842718.mp3",
 "Gravity, motors, wind, springs — add up every force acting on every body.": "61ccb2bd2b17.mp3",
 "Step 2: Integrate.": "33ec2939845c.mp3",
 "Turn forces into new velocities and positions over one small timestep, dt.": "51dce9ff1b0e.mp3",
 "Step 3: Detect collisions.": "3465a2656168.mp3",
 "A cheap broad phase finds pairs that might touch; a precise narrow phase checks them.": "5f0809da93e5.mp3",
 "Step 4: Solve constraints.": "2bb94204e3c4.mp3",
 "Push overlapping bodies apart, keep joints together, apply friction and bounce.": "7886e9410677.mp3",
 "Step 5: Advance time.": "3106ffbe436b.mp3",
 "Record the new state, move the clock forward by dt — and repeat.": "73e71bba5e05.mp3",
